<section class="process-section site-section" aria-labelledby="process-heading">
  <div class="site-container">
    <div class="process-layout">
      <div class="process-intro">
        <span class="section-kicker">How we work together</span>
        <h2 id="process-heading">A plan for the week you actually have.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">You work directly with me, with room to talk through your questions. We turn your priorities into a practical plan, then use weekly check-ins to review what happened and decide what comes next.</p>
      </div>
      <ol class="process-steps">
        <li>
          <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <div><h3>Start with the whole picture.</h3><p>A goal-setting conversation covers your priorities, current routines and responsibilities. Together, we decide what deserves attention first.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <div><h3>Make it workable.</h3><p>Talk through the options, the reasoning behind them and any uncertainty. We build clear actions around your schedule and consider what a demanding week could change.</p></div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="step-number" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <div><h3>Check in. Adjust. Keep going.</h3><p>Weekly check-ins give us a regular point to review and adapt. You also have direct support through an agreed channel. We agree the format, timing and response expectations before enrollment.</p></div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <aside class="planning-example" aria-labelledby="example-heading">
      <div class="example-intro">
        <p class="example-label">Illustrative planning example</p>
        <h3 id="example-heading">Travel changes the week.<br />The plan can change with it.</h3>
        <p>The details would depend on your goals and circumstances.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="example-decisions">
        <div><dt>The starting point</dt><dd>You planned regular gym sessions and an evening routine. Travel removes gym access, and meetings run late.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>What we review</dt><dd>At the check-in, we look at what was manageable, what got in the way and what deserves attention next.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>A possible adjustment</dt><dd>The next plan might use shorter movement sessions, a simple food routine and a more workable bedtime window.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </aside>
    <div class="planning-resource">
      <div>
        <h3>Put your own week on paper.</h3>
        <p>A simple worksheet to choose one priority, plan for a difficult day and review what happened.</p>
      </div>
      <a href="/resources/demanding-week-planning-sheet.pdf" download>Get the planning sheet <span>PDF · 2 pages · no signup</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

